{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","id":"pg_c56b9c5c4fc45b00a5dbd03de2329493","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/tmcfarlane-oh-my-cursor-docs-e2e-test-md-5bad458bff4c-d03de2329493.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_25f726b1881d5e5186100f97c80534e5"],"title":"tmcfarlane/oh-my-cursor/docs/E2E-TEST.md @ 5bad458bff4c","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","updated_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_175a675379fb5ebfae4db9c351020961944ce3f75e6259db51a1a75ae6e0d90d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"19 community-sourced skills are vendored in-repo as SKILL.md directories that Cursor auto-discovers, installed by default with a --no-skills option to skip them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_218c206cdf72a2a5a326ac004db0c58386493041add66c49c1bd7dd5cf4f0c2e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Slash commands map to agents: /plan (Sokka), /build (Aang), /search (Toph), /fix (Katara), /tasks (Appa), /scout (Momo), /doc (Iroh), /image (Zuko), and /cactus-juice (swarm)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_22d5c6340e728f553e5e992f22048e97181d9668881f11cfb8792ebfac3c00a5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Per-agent model routing uses Cursor's model: frontmatter field; the default is composer-2.5-fast, with Sokka and Iroh on claude-opus-4-8-thinking-high and Zuko on gemini-3.1-pro."},{"claim_ids":["clm_28235d4db184be1f31a9edae28411c37017f841f75d732636de60e280a4979d8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The installer supports user (default ~/.cursor) and project (./.cursor) scopes, plus --claude/--codex cross-tool installs, --dry-run, --force, --uninstall, and --disable/--enable orchestration flags."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2c206cd08c2fabaeead0b2d3451a0e6333cf7a9d79f545d6a15205347648ff82"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors clone the repo and run bash install.sh (or install.ps1 on Windows) to install from source; changes to agents, rules, commands, or hooks take effect after reinstalling."},{"claim_ids":["clm_50699e2f38d65fcdd6fd4838f1ea70160d72f821a047ca6018945507c6ceacdd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On Cursor 3.4+ a two-tier swarm pattern applies: coordinators (Aang, Sokka, Katara, Appa) spawn worker agents (Toph, Momo) as leaf nodes with max depth 2; Zuko is root-only."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57651503d8478abd2c8bef4b5f0f2dc31262c0eeb8dbc9da2b1fd86d722e3671"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A '/cactus-juice' swarm mode decomposes requests into 5-10 independent single-file micro-tasks and spawns up to 10 parallel fast-model subagents, with the root collecting and verifying results."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57bb1ec049a4b97399cd70947302af05245d4e61bccf10c0e369a52d2df1918f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A permissions.json auto-review policy auto-runs safe calls (lints, tests, builds, read-only git) and holds risky ones (destructive filesystem, history rewrites, credential access, outbound network) for review."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6da49be344dcd27065b82a9c85f22c10cca84912cc0b39e3a9b56eb6ed7fc0b4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states hooks and auto-review are best-effort and not a security boundary, reducing footguns and approval spam without replacing real sandboxing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7cb6ed239ff8b943c9be60f56704dec43f47c49a25732229f61c4032a72f9b78"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The orchestrator rule makes the root thread a pure dispatcher whose only permitted tools are Task, TodoWrite, AskQuestion, and SwitchMode, delegating all work to specialist agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_843034a99a7e9a0c48e2ea18d0d59ff954b90d2711a91d5dc7cc2f097d36756d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hooks wired via .cursor/hooks.json include guard-shell.sh, which blocks destructive shell commands and commits containing anti-patterns like 'as any' or '@ts-ignore', returning allow/deny/ask decisions on beforeShellExecution."},{"claim_ids":["clm_911d9c9bd8f5e4a4a42658eb309c648c1814ba4608ba475e03839058f46bcbf8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project ships 8 agent manifests, 8 slash commands, hooks, and one orchestration rule as pure Markdown/config files for Cursor, with no external runtime or wrapper CLI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c1693add8051da1924624812cf80bf10efe56b6a4e275d472bd5c203f4e35094"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"docs/E2E-TEST.md is described as a 15-check runbook (model routing, hook enforcement, auto-review) run attended against a live Cursor app, producing a pass/fail table; v0.4.1 validation moved from 13/15 to 15/15 on Cursor 3.9.8."},{"claim_ids":["clm_df796cde9d43da13b49cce5f3477cfbdaae861f3e215bf17c2befbdc90e5e277"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An invalid model slug does not error but silently falls back to composer-2.5-fast, so a typo can make an agent run the wrong model unnoticed; slugs also change between Cursor versions."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ff47ac7fd69edc911c5fe8b48e1923fc1a6d1356c594426f8fbdfa8eba518abe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Requires Cursor 3.4+ with agent mode (subagents); the project is MIT licensed and validated against Cursor 3.8.23 and 3.9.8 per its badges and changelog."}],"claim_ids":["clm_175a675379fb5ebfae4db9c351020961944ce3f75e6259db51a1a75ae6e0d90d","clm_218c206cdf72a2a5a326ac004db0c58386493041add66c49c1bd7dd5cf4f0c2e","clm_22d5c6340e728f553e5e992f22048e97181d9668881f11cfb8792ebfac3c00a5","clm_28235d4db184be1f31a9edae28411c37017f841f75d732636de60e280a4979d8","clm_2c206cd08c2fabaeead0b2d3451a0e6333cf7a9d79f545d6a15205347648ff82","clm_50699e2f38d65fcdd6fd4838f1ea70160d72f821a047ca6018945507c6ceacdd","clm_57651503d8478abd2c8bef4b5f0f2dc31262c0eeb8dbc9da2b1fd86d722e3671","clm_57bb1ec049a4b97399cd70947302af05245d4e61bccf10c0e369a52d2df1918f","clm_6da49be344dcd27065b82a9c85f22c10cca84912cc0b39e3a9b56eb6ed7fc0b4","clm_7cb6ed239ff8b943c9be60f56704dec43f47c49a25732229f61c4032a72f9b78","clm_843034a99a7e9a0c48e2ea18d0d59ff954b90d2711a91d5dc7cc2f097d36756d","clm_911d9c9bd8f5e4a4a42658eb309c648c1814ba4608ba475e03839058f46bcbf8","clm_c1693add8051da1924624812cf80bf10efe56b6a4e275d472bd5c203f4e35094","clm_df796cde9d43da13b49cce5f3477cfbdaae861f3e215bf17c2befbdc90e5e277","clm_ff47ac7fd69edc911c5fe8b48e1923fc1a6d1356c594426f8fbdfa8eba518abe"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:26:36Z","created_by_operation":"op_778ae61339d649c19b0d6086f2044915","id":"pg_d068923c33e059248b0dd8d976c4561e","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/tmcfarlane-oh-my-cursor-readme-md-5bad458bff4c-d8d976c4561e